# Testing

## Commands

- Use `bun run test` for the Vitest suite (`test:unit` / `test:browser` / `test:watch` for scoped runs).
- Do not use `bun test` here — it invokes Bun's runner instead of this project's Vitest config.

## Projects

Vitest runs two projects:

| Project | Files | Environment |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `unit` | `src/**/*.test.ts` | Node |
| `browser` | `src/**/*.test.tsx` | Chromium via Playwright (`@vitest/browser-playwright`) |

- Put pure logic and mocked-API tests in `*.test.ts`.
- Put React component, hook, and route tests in `*.test.tsx` so they run in a real browser.
- Prefer `vitest-browser-react` (`render`, locators, `expect.element`) for component UI assertions.
- `@testing-library/react` `renderHook` is fine for hook-only browser tests.
- Do not add jsdom/happy-dom; browser coverage belongs in the browser project (and later Playwright E2E).

## MSW

- Browser tests start the MSW service worker from `src/testing/setup-browser.ts`.
- Use the browser worker for local app development only behind `VITE_ENABLE_API_MOCKING=true`.
- Full end-to-end flows against a real backend belong in a future Playwright E2E suite, not Vitest Browser Mode.
